g&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lee_Areum_in_Vietnam,_on_Nov_29,_2012.jpg","author":"Monkey Man","license":"CC BY 2.0"},"bio":{"text":"T-ara is a South Korean girl group formed in 2009, currently consisting of four members: Qri, Eunjung, Hyomin, and Jiyeon. T-ara's career is marked by hook-heavy dance-pop music, a result of their close partnership with composer Shinsadong Tiger. They have been referred to as the \"Chameleons of K-pop\" for their versatile concepts and experimentation with musical genres. The group achieved commercial success in several regions in Asia including South Korea and China, and their single \"Roly-Poly\" (2011) became one of the most downloaded domestic singles since 2011 and the most downloaded girl group single to date. T-ara made their debut with the single \"Lies\" in 2009.","title":"Lee Areum","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lee_Areum"}},"Q110115953":{"id":"Q110115953","name":"IF","ko":"","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kang Se-chan"],"birth":"1999-12-16","death":"","birthplace":"","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","rapper","dancer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q97224058","name":"N.cus","start":"","end":""}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q11244337":{"id":"Q11244337","name":"Verbal Jint","ko":"버벌진트","birthName":"김진태","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1980-12-19","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","songwriter","record producer","rapper"],"debut":"1999","agencies":[{"name":"Brand New Music","id":"Q12599305","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[],"links":{"x":"https://x.com/freevj","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/24sQuJhQ85ZygDG7sUVUxR","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/02631a80-5a17-40af-b3fc-eb1aeeffc55d"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kim Jin-tae, better known by his stage name Verbal Jint (버벌진트), is a South 